{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790291238,"nonce":"uPuOR/lbxOfLH5g7lVLUZS8zrnE=","title":"HXSL shaders from other languages","message":"An HXSL shader class should be usable from every language that imports Haxe classes, with the gpu plugin. Found while testing it from Wren: the shader's constants were static inline, so they did not exist at run time; Wren had no way to make a buffer to upload, only to fill one a plugin gave it; and the Wren loader looked for a module of Wren's own namespace (wren:scale) under a wren/ directory, though the bridge names a root-level file that way. The Zyntax languages cannot import another language's classes yet (pending in the Zyntax adapter, docs/architecture/zyntax.md), so they cannot use a shader class.","files":null}]}